## 1. Clean public exports

Currently `src/lib.rs:1–5` exposes these module paths:

```rust
ferox::models::CompletionRequest
ferox::gateway::Gateway
ferox::ports::llm::LlmProvider
```

This makes your internal organisation part of the public API. If you later move `models.rs`, users’ imports break.

A flatter API would allow:

```rust
use ferox::{
    CompletionRequest,
    Gateway,
    LlmProvider,
};
```

You achieve that with `pub use` in `lib.rs`, while making the implementation modules private:

```rust
mod gateway;
mod models;
mod ports;

pub use gateway::Gateway;
pub use models::CompletionRequest;
pub use ports::llm::LlmProvider;
```

This is mainly about **making future refactoring safer**.

## 2. `Model` still needs the same treatment

`Model` is currently at `src/models.rs:2`:

```rust
pub struct Model {
    pub id: String,
    pub input_modalities: Vec<ModelModality>,
    pub output_modalities: Vec<ModelModality>,
}
```

It is missing `#[non_exhaustive]`. If you add a field later, callers using struct literals break.

Add:

```rust
#[non_exhaustive]
pub struct Model {
    // fields...
}
```

Then add a constructor because custom `LlmProvider` implementations need to create `Model` values:

```rust
impl Model {
    pub fn new(
        id: impl Into<String>,
        input_modalities: Vec<ModelModality>,
        output_modalities: Vec<ModelModality>,
    ) -> Self {
        Self {
            id: id.into(),
            input_modalities,
            output_modalities,
        }
    }
}
```

This is about **allowing `Model` to evolve without breaking consumers**.

